module main

-- §9.4: `expect type T` supplies an abstract type-level object WITHOUT
-- ADT constructor metadata; only `expect data` carries deriving support.
-- `derive Eq` against an expect-type has no constructor metadata and
-- must be rejected; the unsatisfied expect is additionally an error in
-- this single-file unit. NOTE: the spec registers no dedicated family
-- for the derive rejection (E_NOT_DATA is unregistered in the harness
-- registry); today the implementation rejects `derive` wholesale with
-- E_UNSUPPORTED. Once derive lands, this must still fail — with a
-- constructor-metadata (not-a-data-type) diagnostic on the derive line.

expect type Ext

derive Eq Ext

--! mode check
--! assertErrorCount 2
--! assertDiagnostic error E_EXPECT_UNSATISFIED
-- STATUS(a51e1bf): PASS
